cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "RIP-seq Analysis Pipeline for Rpb4 Mutants in Saccharomyces cerevisiae"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2025-01-21
authors:
  - family-names: "Hannaoui Anaaoui"
    given-names: "Adil"
abstract: >-
  A complete RIP-seq analysis pipeline for studying RNA-protein interactions
  mediated by the Rpb4 subunit of RNA polymerase II in Saccharomyces cerevisiae.
  The pipeline implements a triple analytical approach — featureCounts-based quantification,
  sliding window analysis, and peak calling — enabling robust identification of
  Rpb4-associated transcripts at multiple levels of resolution. The workflow covers
  end-to-end processing including quality control, read alignment, and all three
  downstream enrichment strategies applied in parallel.Data generated from three
  biological replicates of Rpb4 immunoprecipitation at the Institute of Functional
  Biology and Genomics (IBFG).
keywords:
  - RIP-seq
  - Saccharomyces cerevisiae
  - Rpb4
  - RNA polymerase II
  - differential expression
  - DESeq2
  - bioinformatics
  - genomics
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AdilHannaoui/RIP-seq-Analysis"
url: "https://github.com/AdilHannaoui/RIP-seq-Analysis"
